---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import Timeline from "../components/Timeline.astro";
import profile from "../data/profile.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Saroj Baral's background in electronics and communication engineering, 6 years at Huawei Technologies Nepal in project control, EMBA, and freelance operations consulting."
>
  <div class="site-container section-padding">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <span
        class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-2"
      >
        Background &amp; Philosophy
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-text)] mb-6"
      >
        About
      </h1>

      <p
        class="text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] leading-relaxed font-medium"
      >
        From <span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold"
          >electronics engineering</span
        > to multinational project management and business studies, my journey has
        shaped one core interest: <span
          class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold"
          >making information reliable, meaningful, and actionable.</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Three Story Blocks -->
    <div
      class="max-w-3xl space-y-10 text-[var(--color-text)] leading-relaxed mb-16"
    >
      <!-- Story Block 1 -->
      <section class="card-base p-6 md:p-8 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3 text-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          Engineering Foundation
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base mb-3">
          My technical journey began with a Bachelor's Degree in Electronics
          &amp; Communication Engineering from Kathmandu Engineering College.
          Early hands-on roles at Radio Nepal analyzing transmission equipment
          and at GTL Nepal conducting technical assessments across
          telecommunication BTS sites taught me the discipline of systematic
          field data collection.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base">
          Working directly with broadcast transmitters and BTS infrastructure
          demonstrated how minor data discrepancies at the site level compound
          into severe operational blindspots. That technical grounding
          established a lifelong respect for verified, empirical data over
          assumptions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Story Block 2 -->
      <section class="card-base p-6 md:p-8 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3 text-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          Huawei Technologies Nepal (2013–2019)
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base mb-3">
          For six years at Huawei Technologies Nepal, I served as Engineer and
          Manager within Technical Solution, Project Control &amp; Operations.
          My primary mandate was maintaining ERP data integrity and producing
          project performance reports for senior executive leadership.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base mb-3">
          I consolidated high-volume operational inputs across sales, finance,
          supply chain, delivery teams, and external subcontractors—relentlessly
          following up to close documentation gaps. I led material planning and
          inventory coordination based on Bill of Quantities (BOQ) and SCM
          systems, implemented change-control protocols, and tracked issue
          resolution across multi-million dollar rollouts.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base">
          This rigor earned multiple team recognitions, including Outstanding
          Achievement in Customer Satisfaction, Project Office Business Skill
          Authentication, Employee of the Month, and a Certificate of Merit at
          the WDM Golden Seeds Training in Shenzhen.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Story Block 3 -->
      <section class="card-base p-6 md:p-8 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3 text-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          Business + Independence (2019–present)
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base mb-3">
          Recognizing that operational data issues are fundamentally business
          problems, I completed my Executive MBA at Himalayan WhiteHouse
          International College between 2019 and 2022. The program deepened my
          understanding of managerial finance, operations strategy, and
          organizational decision-making.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base">
          Since 2022, I have operated as an independent consultant helping small
          and medium enterprises bring enterprise-grade structure to their
          reporting workflows. I design practical Excel MIS systems, standardize
          document registers, optimize fulfillment pipelines, and provide
          hands-on project coordination support.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Career Timeline -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <SectionHeading
        eyebrow="Chronology"
        title="Experience & Career History"
        intro="A detailed summary of corporate, consulting, and engineering roles."
      />
      <Timeline />
    </div>

    <!-- How I Work -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <SectionHeading
        eyebrow="Operating Principles"
        title="How I work"
        intro="Four principles that guide every consulting engagement and internal reporting setup."
      />
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="card-base p-5 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-1"
            >01</span
          >
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">
            Structure first
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
            A clean, verified tracker beats a clever or fragile macro-heavy
            sheet every time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-base p-5 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-1"
            >02</span
          >
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">
            Define "done" before starting
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
            Agree explicitly on the exact output format, required fields, and
            sign-off criteria.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-base p-5 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-1"
            >03</span
          >
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">
            Write it down; follow up on gaps
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
            Unrecorded assumptions create disputes. Keep single-source registers
            and close discrepancies promptly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-base p-5 bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
          <span class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-1"
            >04</span
          >
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">
            Hand over something you can maintain
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
            A system is only successful if your existing team can run it
            confidently after handover.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Beyond Work -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl card-base p-6 md:p-8 bg-[var(--color-surface)] mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">
        Beyond work
      </h3>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Based in Bhaktapur, Nepal. Volunteer in 2015 earthquake relief and
        reconstruction — shelter, homes, schools, sanitation, health camps.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-border)]">
        <span
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-accent)] block mb-2"
          >Languages:</span
        >
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text)]">
          {
            profile.languages.map((lang) => (
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-border)] text-xs font-medium">
                {lang.name} ({lang.level})
              </span>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTAs -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <a href="/cv" class="btn-base btn-primary text-sm px-5 py-2.5">
        Download CV
      </a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-base btn-secondary text-sm px-5 py-2.5">
        Contact me &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
